§ `The duties as regulative rules`

-- The text states a period and no consequence of missing it.  "MUST" without a LEST defaults
-- to BREACH, which here means only "the period was missed" (fork F13).  The clock of a trace
-- is in days from the day the period starts: AT 0 is the notification day, AT 30 the last
-- day of a 30-day period, AT 31 is late.  No suspension is modelled in a trace.
-- src:63 | 1 Die Beschwerde gegen einen Entscheid ist innert 30 Tagen nach der Eröffnung der vollständigen Ausfertigung beim Bundesgericht einzureichen.
@ref Art. 100(1) BGG (the duty) (src:63)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor in chapter 4` `Act in chapter 4`
`Art 100(1) the appellant's duty to file the appeal within 30 days` MEANS
    PARTY Appellant
    MUST `file the appeal with the Federal Supreme Court`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Appellant BECAUSE "the appeal was not filed within 30 days after the complete version of the decision was notified"

